A cylinder has a uniform cross-section, but it is a circle, so a cylinder is **not** a prism.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw (-1.8,0)--(-1.8,4);
\draw (1.8,0)--(1.8,4);
\draw (0,4) ellipse (1.8 and 0.55);
\draw (-1.8,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=1.8,y radius=0.55];
\draw[dashed] (-1.8,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,x radius=1.8,y radius=0.55];
\draw[red,dashed,thick] (0,2) ellipse (1.8 and 0.55);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

